# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys.
#
# LOCAL ONLY, and the only place a key belongs.
#
# Neither deployed app has an API route, so neither can reach a provider no
# matter what is set on it — which is a stronger guarantee than any permission
# check in this repository, because it is the absence of a capability rather
# than a rule about one. Recording happens on a laptop; the results are
# published by committing public/runs/ and pushing.
#
# Verify the deployment with ./verify-deployment.sh <harness-url> [gym-url].
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# The environment to drive. Defaults to the deployed gym; point it at a local
# clickmail while you are working on one.
# GYM_URL=http://localhost:3000/gym

# Spending is opt-in, bounded, and per invocation. Left unset, every request
# carries a zero price ceiling that the provider enforces by refusing rather
# than billing. Naming a paid model without a budget exits before the browser
# starts.
#   BUDGET=0.30 MODEL=google/gemini-3.7-flash MODE=both ./record-runs.sh
